e86c9d-f777-5ade-ba76-e4af97e240d4" 13194139535282 true] [17592186341521 1145 "The binomial theorem for positive integer $n$ states that\n\n$$\n(a+b)^{n}=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{0}){a}^{n}{b}^{0}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{1}){a}^{n-1}{b}^{1}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{2}){a}^{n-2}{b}^{2}+…+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{n}){a}^{0}{b}^{n}.\n$$\n\nBy substituting $a=4,$ $b=x,$ and $n=4,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(4+x)}^{4} & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{0}){(4)}^{4}{(x)}^{0}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{1}){(4)}^{4-1}{(x)}^{1}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{2}){(4)}^{4-2}{(x)}^{2}+⋯ \\\\  & =1{(4)}^{4}+4{(4)}^{3}{(x)}^{1}+6{(4)}^{2}{(x)}^{2}+⋯ \\\\  & =256+4(64)(x)+6(16)({x}^{2})+⋯ \\\\  & =256+256x+96{x}^{2}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for small $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n{(4+x)}^{4}≈256+256x+96{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $x=-0.01$ into the above approximation of $(4+x)^{4}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3.99)^{4} & =(4+(-0.01))^{4} \\\\  & ≈256+256(-0.01)+96(-0.01)^{2} \\\\  & =256-256(0.01)+96(0.000\\,1) \\\\  & =256-2.56+0.009\\,6 \\\\  & =253.450,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto three decimal places." 13194139535282 true] [17592186341522 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341523 13194139535282 true] [17592186341522 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341524 13194139535282 true] [17592186341522 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341525 13194139535282 true] [17592186341522 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341526 13194139535282 true] [17592186341522 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341527 13194139535282 true] [17592186341522 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535282 true] [17592186341522 1041 "selection" 13194139535282 true] [17592186341522 1104 #edb/ref 17592186341527 13194139535282 true] [17592186341522 1110 #uuid "1ced7d05-d001-504d-a4ea-3b543c3c491a" 13194139535282 true] [17592186341523 1034 "253.412" 13194139535282 true] [17592186341523 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535282 true] [17592186341523 1111 #uuid "a1b2a2a7-0975-5e41-a146-b457e9f896ac" 13194139535282 true] [17592186341524 1034 "253.589" 13194139535282 true] [17592186341524